{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779728990,"nonce":"1Pysc70M0EAAIB60zYUO5uB6d0M=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDVJq0g","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/174","origin":"github"},"title":"Audit agent transcripts vs committed deployment logs; backfill un-captured info","message":"## Context\nThe committed deployment logs (`docs/logs/`) are the durable record, but every deployment runs as a long agent conversation in which the operator mentions observations and agents discover findings *in-session*. Relevant info discussed there can fail to reach the committed log.\n\n**Motivating near-miss (2026-05-25):** while setting up the #167 power analysis we needed the boat's idle current. A first (truncated) search concluded it had \"never been measured\" — but it had: the operator told an agent the **base current at rest ≈ 8 A** during the 2026-04-27 deployment, and it *did* land in `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-27_dev_logs.md:1291` (with a full coulomb-counting SOC model). It was recovered from the Claude Code session transcripts. The scare showed how easily an operator-mentioned value or an agent finding could be lost between conversation and committed log.\n\n## Goal\nSystematically review the agent session transcripts from the deployment-logging era (~2026-04-24 → present) and cross-check them against the committed daily logs; **backfill any operator-mentioned observation or agent-discovered finding** (measurements, decisions, anomalies, bug observations, config readings) that did not make it.\n\n## Scope / method\n- **Transcripts:** `~/.claude/projects/-home-roland-project11{,-jazzy}/**/*.jsonl` (dev-side, incl. subagent transcripts). Field-host agent transcripts (gabby / salmon) are separate and may warrant their own pass if reachable.\n- **Logs:** `docs/logs/2026/\u003cdate\u003e_\u003clabel\u003e_logs.md`.\n- Per deployment day: extract operator observations + agent findings from the transcript(s), check presence in that day's log, produce a **gap list**, then backfill into the appropriate daily log.\n- Backfill **factual context only**; honor sensitive-info constraints (e.g. keep the Lake Massabesic mission low-key — never to repo docs) and do not reference private agent-memory filenames in repo docs.\n\n## Deliverable\nPer-day gap list + backfill PR(s). Phaseable per deployment. Relates to the workspace deployment-logging capability tracker [`rolker/ros2_agent_workspace#477`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_agent_workspace/issues/477) and the log convention in `docs/logs/README.md`.","files":null}]}